# Line endings, settled in the repository rather than per machine.
#
# Prettier is configured `endOfLine: lf` (.prettierrc.json), so a CRLF working
# tree fails `npm run format:check` on every file at once. That is exactly what
# happened on a Windows clone: `core.autocrlf=true` rewrote 323 files to CRLF on
# checkout, and format:check went from clean to 254 failures without a single
# line of code changing. CI never saw it, because CI checks out on Linux.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND checks out LF
# everywhere, so the setting travels with the clone instead of depending on each
# developer's `core.autocrlf`. Binary files are detected automatically and left
# alone; the explicit list below is belt and braces for the ones already in the
# tree, since a corrupted PNG is a slow thing to notice.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
